# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table II (MAE and RMSE of energies and forces by system, level and potential) is not in the extracted text as numbers. The text gives averages over the four systems for the pre-robust potentials only: energy MAE (RMSE) of 27 (44), 16 (25) and 8 (13) meV/atom and force MAE (RMSE) of 75 (217), 51 (147) and 26 (78) meV/A for levels 10, 16 and 22. Since these are averages over systems and belong to the pre-robust stage, no AccuracyMetric is attached to the per-system runs.
# - Each system and level has three potentials (pre-robust, robust, accurate); one run per system and level stands for the robust potential. No level-22 potential is reported for C-Mo-W.
# - The data sets are declared with provenance Augmented (published AFLOW data plus new DFT single points). The AFLOW relaxation data come with AFLOW's own settings; the reference node describes the calculations of this work.
# - Convex-hull reproduction and discovery of new stable structures are the paper's main results and have no MetricProperty. Relaxation with the MTPs is the ground for GeometryOptimization.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
